.TH LOOMD 1 "June 2026" "loom 0.3.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loomd \- Loom background daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loomd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loomd
is the background daemon that aggregates the Loom subsystem crates
(skills, MCP, sessions, auth, hooks, workflow, routing, knowledge,
telemetry, etc.) and exposes them over a Unix domain socket so the
.BR loom (1)
CLI and other clients can talk to a single long\-lived process instead
of paying startup cost on every invocation.
.PP
The daemon reads its configuration from
.BR ~/.loom/config.toml
(plus any layer overlays under
.BR ~/.loom/config/ ),
stores per\-crate state in
.BR ~/.loom/ ,
and emits events on the cross\-process ZeroMQ socket
.BR ~/.loom/.loom-events
when built with the
.B cross-process
feature.
.PP
If the daemon receives no IPC traffic for
.B DAEMON_DEFAULT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS
(5 minutes by default), it shuts itself down.
.SH OPTIONS
The daemon currently takes no command line options; it reads its
configuration from
.BR ~/.loom/config.toml .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.loom/config.toml
Main configuration.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/config/
Optional per\-subsystem configuration overlays
(\fBrouting.toml\fR, \fBmcp.toml\fR, \fBhooks.toml\fR, \fBacp.toml\fR).
.TP
.B ~/.loom/loomd.sock
The Unix domain socket the daemon listens on.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/.loom-events
The ZeroMQ socket used to broadcast cross\-process events.
.TP
.BR ~/.loom/.cache/ " (or \fB$CACHE_DIR\fR)"
Snapshot cache used to keep cold starts below the 50ms budget.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Initiate graceful shutdown: stop accepting new connections, drain
in\-flight requests, then exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown after a
.BR SIGINT / SIGTERM
or after the idle timeout fires.
.TP
.B non\-zero
Startup error (could not bind the socket, configuration could not be
parsed, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loom (1)
.PP
